# .orchestrate — what the orchestrate skill needs to know about this repo.
# Plain bash, sourced by the kit from the repo root. Everything is optional;
# JS repos get a default from package.json when a value is missing. A value
# set in the environment of a bootstrap or add-lane call wins over this file.
#
# Your own run defaults for every repo go in the user contract,
# ${XDG_CONFIG_HOME:-~/.config}/tower/orchestrate, in the same syntax. It may
# set only the kinds, the per-kind models, STALE, the method and review
# switches and the credit guard; anything else it names on stderr and
# ignores. Precedence: the call's environment, then this file, then the user
# contract, then the kit's model-defaults.

# The check gate: one command every lane must pass before it commits a task.
CHECK_CMD="bun run check"

# What add-lane.sh runs in each new lane's worktree. Default: the package
# manager's install (bun install, npm install, ...), and nothing at all when
# the repo has no package.json. INSTALL_CMD= turns the install off.
# INSTALL_CMD="bun install --frozen-lockfile"

# Panes on the bottom row, running in lane A's checkout (the integration branch).
#   pane NAME "COMMAND" [DIR]     NAME is checks or dev; DIR is relative to the checkout.
pane checks "bun test --watch"
# pane dev  "bun run dev" apps/web

# The lanes' harness (kind): claude (default), codex or cursor (cursor-agent).
# EXECUTOR_KIND=cursor for one lane only goes in that add-lane call, so a run
# can mix kinds.
# EXECUTOR_KIND=cursor
# EXECUTOR_MODEL replaces the model of every lane of this repo's runs, of
# whichever kind: pair it with the kind it names. The per-kind keys below
# suit a mixed run.
# EXECUTOR_MODEL=gpt-6-astra

# Model defaults, per kind. The kit's own are in
# skills/orchestrate/model-defaults (the values shown); set a key here, or in
# the user contract, to change it.
# EXECUTOR_MODEL_CLAUDE='claude-opus-5-5[1m]'
# EXECUTOR_MODEL_CODEX=gpt-6-astra
# EXECUTOR_MODEL_CURSOR=grok-4.7-high-fast
# The Reviewer's model, per the Reviewer's kind. _CLAUDE_SELF is claude
# reviewing a claude lane; a codex Reviewer of a codex lane runs on the
# lane's model.
# REVIEWER_MODEL_CLAUDE=claude-opus-5-5
# REVIEWER_MODEL_CODEX=gpt-6-astra
# REVIEWER_MODEL_CURSOR=grok-4.7-high-fast
# REVIEWER_MODEL_CLAUDE_SELF=claude-fable-5-1

# The spec and quality reviewer models: tower records them for the run, and
# each lane's per-task reviews use them. Defaults per the run's executor
# kind: sonnet and opus for claude and codex, grok-4.7-high-fast for cursor.
# SPEC_REVIEWER_MODEL=sonnet
# QUALITY_REVIEWER_MODEL=opus
# SPEC_REVIEWER_MODEL_CURSOR=grok-4.7-high-fast
# QUALITY_REVIEWER_MODEL_CURSOR=grok-4.7-high-fast

# Minutes of silence before the console and tower wait flag a lane as stale
# (default 30).
# STALE=30

# The full suite: the repo's thorough checks, run once by preflight on the
# whole branch. Named steps, run in this order, every one even when one fails.
#   suite NAME "COMMAND" [DIR]    DIR is relative to the checkout (default .).
# Without suite lines preflight runs the detected checks, then CHECK_CMD.
# suite lint      "bun run lint"
# suite typecheck "bun run typecheck"
# suite test      "bun test"
# suite build     "bun run build" apps/web

# The run switches. Each line shows the default; the user's message overrides
# them per run in plain words. A value outside the listed ones is refused.
# TASK_REVIEW=on        on | off    the spec and quality review after each task inside a lane
# LANE_REVIEW=on        on | off    a Reviewer reviews each lane's diff before it is merged
# PREFLIGHT=on          on | off    preflight checks the whole branch before the PR
# STATIC_BASELINE=on    on | off    preflight scans the diff with semgrep and gitleaks
# PR=draft              draft | ready | off    how the run's PR is opened, or no PR
# METHOD=tdd            tdd | plain    plain briefs lanes without the tdd loop
# REVIEWER_KIND=other   other | claude | codex | cursor
#                       other: the first installed of the lane's candidates
#                       (claude lane: codex; codex lane: claude; cursor lane:
#                       claude, then codex), else the lane's own kind. cursor
#                       reviews a claude or codex lane only when set here.
# REVIEWER_MODEL=       the Reviewer's model; empty: the kit picks one per kind
# REVIEWER_BY_CREDITS=off
#                       off | on    the credit guard: skip a Reviewer kind
#                       nearly out of quota. On, it reads claude's and
#                       cursor's tokens from the macOS keychain and calls
#                       undocumented endpoints. Unreadable credits count as
#                       enough; each skip is a tower note.
# REVIEWER_CREDITS_MIN=20
#                       0-100: the % left below which the guard skips a kind
# REVIEW_AREAS=         preflight's areas, comma-separated; empty: every area
# SUITE_SKIP=           suite steps to skip, comma-separated (e.g. build)
# PR_TEMPLATE=          a PR body template in the repo; empty: preflight's default
